{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0244", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{X_i \\to S\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$(V_i/X_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{X_i \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$V_i \\to X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-fpqc-covering}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-closed-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b63f5cfadc9587f30a63edb62e9845022dd14241a2e3c7c466534c9f19d0b2ba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d966aceb4920cc865fe9e0a9444f368d4b2f21db65f5f5102e744e89ea7b802a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an fpqc covering, see\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a descent datum\nrelative to <MATH_0004>. If each morphism\n<MATH_0005> is a closed immersion, then the descent datum is\neffective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80da8d9e200baef8d9726b63a2746e16be3366672e5d57f7ab6b01e82d60691e", "unit_id": "tag:03I0:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0244", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-closed-immersion-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91e80f26848c378341f9cb55bfd16dfc86d8eda85049aba8b36e6f59c2fbd415", "source_text": "This is true because a closed immersion is an affine morphism\n(Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>),\nand hence Lemma <REF_0002> applies.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:63ad48c7c75a40bd86571131b16849fd9a625506e5862c83cb1308ad30b89b88", "unit_id": "tag:03I0:proof"}
